        {
          "id": "satoplam-t02-q053",
          "skill": "Details Question",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Locate and interpret specific details explicitly stated in the text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 2 · Q53",
          "passageTitle": "Details Question — Q53",
          "passage": "In 2004, Andrew Rogers created Ancient\nLanguage. In this work, Rogers created an\n80-meter-long geoglyph out of rocks in the\nAtacama Desert. Rogers's work is part of the\nland art movement, in which artists reject the\nconfinement and commercialization of art\ngalleries. These artists usually install large-scale\npieces outdoors, often in surprising locations.",
